## Usage

Put raw CSV files in `data/raw/`, then:

```bash
make pipeline                    # data/raw/*.csv -> data/processed/*.parquet
uv run {{project_slug}} run --json        # the same, with a JSON summary on stdout
uv run marimo edit notebooks/explore.py   # explore the data in marimo's editor
```

<!-- stacks:fill Where the raw data comes from and what each output is used for. -->

Settings come from flags, `{{env_prefix}}_*` environment variables or a `.env` file (see `.env.example`). [docs/data-contract.md](docs/data-contract.md) lists the input columns, the cleaning rules, the outputs and the exit codes.

## Development

Requires [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/) and make.

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `make install` | Create `.venv` and install the project and its dev tools |
| `make lint` / `make format` | Check / fix lint and formatting (ruff, marimo check) |
| `make typecheck` | mypy strict over the package, tests and notebooks |
| `make coverage` | Tests with the coverage floor |
| `make pipeline-check` | Run the pipeline on the fixture and compare with the expected output |
| `make notebooks` | Run every notebook headlessly |

Run `make help` for the full list. [docs/ARCHITECTURE.md](docs/ARCHITECTURE.md) maps the modules.
